    $ts$2025-06-12T09:00:00+07:00$ts$::timestamptz,
    'published',
    $s$fintech-healthcare-coverage$s$,
    $t$Fintech and healthcare lead non-Jakarta coverage requests.$t$,
    $e$Brands in regulated categories are pairing national wire runs with city-level trade and community outlets for trust-building.$e$,
    $st$Fintech and healthcare lead non-Jakarta coverage requests$st$,
    $sd$Brands in regulated categories are pairing national wire runs with city-level trade and community outlets for trust-building.$sd$,
    $c$Sectors$c$,
    $img$https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1576091160399-112ba8d25d1d?w=1400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80$img$,
    $alt$Healthcare professional using a tablet$alt$,
    $an$Nadia Kusuma$an$,
    $ar$Sector editor$ar$,
    $av$https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544005313-94ddf0286df2?w=96&h=96&fit=crop&q=80$av$,
    $body$<p>Fintech and healthcare are leading the briefs that ask for coverage beyond Jakarta. Both categories sell trust as much as they sell a product, and both sit under rules that make a generic lifestyle placement the wrong proof.</p><p>The pattern is a split run. A national business or trade desk still carries the announcement. City-level trade titles and community outlets then carry the version that a customer, a clinic, or a regional partner will actually read.</p><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1576091160399-112ba8d25d1d?w=1400&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80" alt="Healthcare professional using a tablet"><h2>Why the split run works</h2><ul><li><strong>National desks for the announcement.</strong> Headquarters and search still need the canonical story.</li><li><strong>City trade and community outlets for trust.</strong> One without the other looks either too central or too small.</li><li><strong>Cleaner labeling and tighter facts.</strong> Editors in these beats will not stretch a claim, and they will not hide a sponsor line.</li></ul><h2>If you are entering from outside Indonesia</h2><p>Do not borrow a playbook from an unregulated consumer launch. Map the desks that already cover the category, pick the cities where you are actually licensed or launching, and build the mix before the first draft.</p>$body$
  ),
(
    $ts$2025-05-08T09:00:00+07:00$ts$::timestamptz,
    $ts$2025-05-08T09:00:00+07:00$ts$::timestamptz,
    $ts$2025-05-08T09:00:00+07:00$ts$::timestamptz,
    'published',
    $s$national-reach-media-map$s$,
    $t$What “national reach” actually means in Indonesia’s media map.$t$,
    $e$A practical breakdown of online groups, creator tiers, and print/TV partners — and how to mix them without wasting budget.$e$,
    $st$What “national reach” actually means in Indonesia’s media map$st$,
    $sd$A practical breakdown of online groups, creator tiers, and print/TV partners — and how to mix them without wasting budget.$sd$,
    $c$Insights$c$,
    $img$https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1524661135-423995f22d0b?w=1400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80$img$,
    $alt$Map pins on a world map$alt$,
    $an$Budi Santoso$an$,
    $ar$Insights editor$ar$,
    $av$https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500648767791-00dcc994a43e?w=96&h=96&fit=crop&q=80$av$,
    $body$<p>“National reach” is the phrase that shows up in almost every brief. It is also the phrase that hides the most waste. Indonesia is not one audience and it is not one channel. A real map has online groups, creator tiers, and print and TV partners — and they do different jobs.</p><p>Online outlets give you speed, search, and a link you can send to headquarters. Creators give you time-in-feed and a voice that already has an audience in a city or niche. Print and TV still matter when the reader is a regulator, a board, or a household that does not live on a For You page.</p><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1524661135-423995f22d0b?w=1400&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80" alt="Map pins on a world map"><h2>How to mix without wasting budget</h2><ul><li><strong>Let the goal pick the channel.</strong> A product launch that needs Google citations is a different build from a trust campaign in a regulated category.</li><li><strong>Do not buy all three by default.</strong> A city opening outside Java is a third build. Buying everything without a reason is how budgets disappear.</li><li><strong>Start with who has to see the story.</strong> Then pick the outlets and creators that match — not the ones that merely sound national.</li></ul><h2>Looking ahead</h2><p>That is the difference between a report full of logos and a campaign that actually landed.</p>$body$
  )
